WEBVTT

NOTE placeholder captions for B1 from the storyboard narration (temp)

B1-1-1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Six weeks into the engagement, NorthRiver's steering committee meets to review your recommendations.

B1-2-1
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.765
Sarah Chen, the CFO, points at the list.

B1-2-2
00:00:11.765 --> 00:00:16.000
Why the contract tool, and not the leads agent?

B1-3-1
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.360
This is where most engagement reports fail.

B1-3-2
00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:28.000
Their recommendations trace back to nothing, so the only answer is that it seemed like a good idea.

B1-4-1
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.429
Now the same question, answered from a card.

B1-4-2
00:00:31.429 --> 00:00:40.000
Behind the contract tool is a pain: two contracts renewed by themselves, and one of them cost forty thousand dollars.

B1-5-1
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:50.000
Behind the pain is Robert Pak, the person who feels it, his own words, and the interview where he said them, with its date.

B1-6-1
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.381
Every pain becomes a card.

B1-6-2
00:00:52.381 --> 00:00:53.333
No exceptions.

B1-6-3
00:00:53.333 --> 00:00:56.667
From here on you run the math.

B1-6-4
00:00:56.667 --> 00:01:00.000
Don't let the math forget the value.
